From 6827e1bb380282aa7d85795e85a8173479d5aaa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hizuru254 <2654837056@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:34:02 +0800
Subject: [01/14] protocol v1.3: regional equilibration, per-step heat
 injection, reservoir inset

Fixes four independent causes of the non-linear / inverted temperature profile
found on the WSL2 machine (R^2 0.009-0.94, "-z" hot reservoir colder than
"+z" cold reservoir). Potentials, layer order, QC thresholds and the flux
definition are unchanged.

R1 fix heat N: the template passed the group atom count (1728) where LAMMPS
   expects the injection interval, i.e. 1.728 eV pulses every 1.728 ps.
   Now N=1; flux symmetry 2.3% -> 0.0000.
R2 reservoirs sat on the free Si surfaces, which reach 600-750 K during NVT
   equilibration; build_geometry.py --res-inset 8 moves them 8 A inside.
R3 a single global NVT cannot remove an internal gradient (it constrains only
   the total kinetic energy); template in.pattern.v13.template thermostats the
   two halves separately during equilibration.
R4 R^2 >= 0.995 is unattainable here: the bulk drop inside a 16 A window is
   ~0.2 K while a 2 A bin carries ~1.2 K standard error. Added
   tools/tbr_uncertainty.py (block-averaged TBR +- sigma); the gate is kept
   as-is and both readings are reported.

New tooling
  tools/scan_parallel.py   batch driver pinned to disjoint CPU sets, honours the
                           measured WSL2 ceiling of 48 concurrent MPI ranks
                           (56-64 ranks collapse from ~128 to 3-7 steps/s)
  tools/tbr_uncertainty.py TBR with block-averaged uncertainty and per-interface SNR
  tools/rank_scan.py       ranked table of all runs in a workspace
  build_geometry.py        --res-inset; fix double-sided left Ti etch (the whole
                           Ti layer was being deleted, Ti 9724 -> 17498)

Measurements (docs/PROTOCOL_V13.md, docs/STATUS_20261112.md)
  * lmp 29 Sep 2021 U2, OpenMPI 4.1.2, python 3.10.12 / numpy 1.21.5
  * lmp 29Sep2021 has no -nonbuf; removed from run_seed.sh
  * potential hashes identical to the Windows originals (lock rebuilt)
  * linear response verified: TBR(1 eV/ps)=1.93e-9+-0.44e-9,
    TBR(3 eV/ps)=2.17e-9+-0.24e-9
  * 13-point pattern scan + flat control at 60 ps (reports/scan_ranking_*)
  * 200 ps validation shows TBR is NOT converged: it rises monotonically
    (P350 1.21e-9 at 20 ps -> 4.23e-9 at 160 ps) because interface relaxation
    releases 0.1-0.9 eV/ps, comparable to the imposed flux. The 60 ps ranking
    therefore reverses at 100 ps; no "best pattern" is claimed.
